1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,263
None of these three places

2
00:00:01,293 --> 00:00:02,545
on Earth are CGI.

3
00:00:03,281 --> 00:00:05,084
The last one drowns human lungs

4
00:00:05,114 --> 00:00:06,112
from the inside.

5
00:00:06,326 --> 00:00:07,644
At midnight in Indonesia,

6
00:00:07,764 --> 00:00:09,364
Kawah Ijen volcano appears

7
00:00:09,394 --> 00:00:11,443
to pour rivers of electric-blue lava.

8
00:00:12,187 --> 00:00:14,052
Except lava is never blue.

9
00:00:14,281 --> 00:00:16,257
Pressurized sulfur gas shoots from cracks

10
00:00:16,287 --> 00:00:17,829
at six hundred degrees Celsius

11
00:00:17,859 --> 00:00:19,580
and ignites on contact with air.

12
00:00:20,333 --> 00:00:22,457
Some gas condenses into liquid sulfur

13
00:00:22,487 --> 00:00:23,979
that keeps burning bright blue

14
00:00:24,009 --> 00:00:25,285
as it flows downhill.

15
00:00:25,509 --> 00:00:27,911
Cross into Ethiopia's Danakil Depression,

16
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:30,301
and Earth stops looking habitable altogether.

17
00:00:31,046 --> 00:00:32,842
At Dallol, shallow volcanic heat

18
00:00:32,872 --> 00:00:34,949
boils groundwater packed with iron salts

19
00:00:34,979 --> 00:00:36,244
and sulfuric acid.

20
00:00:36,469 --> 00:00:39,104
Those neon-green pools drop below zero pH

21
00:00:39,134 --> 00:00:40,460
into negative acidity.

22
00:00:41,213 --> 00:00:42,910
Even with liquid water everywhere,

23
00:00:43,057 --> 00:00:44,401
biologists found zero

24
00:00:44,431 --> 00:00:46,907
active microbial life inside the ponds.

25
00:00:47,155 --> 00:00:49,598
Three hundred meters beneath Naica, Mexico

26
00:00:49,628 --> 00:00:51,333
lies an even stranger trap:

27
00:00:51,405 --> 00:00:52,730
the Cave of the Crystals.

28
00:00:53,475 --> 00:00:55,369
Mineral-rich hot water slowly grew

29
00:00:55,399 --> 00:00:57,219
gypsum beams eleven meters long

30
00:00:57,249 --> 00:00:59,077
and weighing fifty-five tons.

31
00:00:59,323 --> 00:01:01,065
Inside, fifty-eight-degree heat

32
00:01:01,095 --> 00:01:03,013
meets ninety-five percent humidity—

33
00:01:03,127 --> 00:01:04,654
hotter than your own lungs.

34
00:01:05,426 --> 00:01:07,521
Without ice suits and chilled air packs,

35
00:01:07,636 --> 00:01:09,146
every breath condenses water

36
00:01:09,176 --> 00:01:10,867
straight into your airways.

37
00:01:11,638 --> 00:01:13,885
That doesn't mean these places break physics—

38
00:01:14,012 --> 00:01:15,257
extreme heat and acid

39
00:01:15,287 --> 00:01:17,786
simply push chemistry past human limits.

40
00:01:18,024 --> 00:01:20,211
In twenty seventeen, groundwater flooded

41
00:01:20,241 --> 00:01:22,348
the Naica crystal cave shut forever—

42
00:01:22,475 --> 00:01:24,137
leaving three real worlds on Earth

43
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:25,694
that look completely impossible.
